From: Daniel Lehmann <dlehmann@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:09:13 +0200
Subject: Reland "[wasm] Don't authenticate LiftoffSetupFrame calling PC"

This is a reland of commit 3640a862c8e6638fe42235df945b29003d000bd2

Skip the new regression test under `sandbox_hardware_support` in
mjsunit.status, as it uses `console.profile()` which is unsupported
with PKU on Linux kernels older than 6.12 (crbug.com/429173713).

Original change's description:
> [wasm] Don't authenticate LiftoffSetupFrame calling PC
>
> Generate_WasmLiftoffFrameSetup sets the WASM_LIFTOFF_SETUP frame marker
> a few instructions before it signs and spills the calling PC. A profiler
> tick in that window sees a correctly typed frame whose calling PC slot
> is still unsigned, and ComputeCallerState() authenticated it, which
> aborts on arm64 with control flow integrity.
>
> Read the slot unauthenticated instead. It only serves as a lookup key in
> HasTaggedOutgoingParams(), never as a branch target.
>
> Bug: 560536735
> Fixed: 562455563

